<%
  /* Intentional consolidation (WI #269, carried into WI #318 / design v2): this
     template deliberately abstracts the reference SSAD's product-scattered
     Solution Overview deep-dive into a small set of generic support-architecture
     modules/fields — it is NOT a 1:1 heading map to the reference, and that is
     by design. See docs/research/design-definition-reference-reconciliation.md
     §6 and §9, grounded in docs/reconciliation/ssad-reconciliation.md.
     #213 (ADR-0057): the SSAD follows the SAD's reading order and heading names
     rather than the FV Help Tool SSAD reference's. Every chapter up to
     "# Technology architecture" is the SAD's, in the SAD's order, with only the
     fields the SSAD renders; the support-team material then stays together
     under one "# Support and operations" chapter. A field both documents render
     takes the SAD's heading ("Logical components view", "Backup and archiving
     policy"), except "Stakeholders and support contacts", which keeps its
     support-facing name — see definition.yaml's `ssad.requires` comment.
     Blank-field guard `na()` is injected once as an Eta functionHeader by
     lib/render.js (WI #273 / R2). A `module.field?` requires entry is in scope
     but not gate-blocking (WI #276), so it renders as a suppress-when-blank
     `<% if %>` section; every other field here is bare (gate-blocking) and
     rendered via na(). #214: the Overview chapter carries
     `introduction.overview`, and a "# Design basis" chapter follows it when
     `assumptions` or `constraints` is filled, inlined as in the SAD rather than
     via `_designBasisOptional.md.tmpl` (the SSAD's scope is those two fields,
     not the partial's five). */
  const dsc = it.modules['data-security-controls'] || {}
